The voice assistant downloads and runs these third-party models. They are not stored in this repository; each one
is fetched at a pinned version and checked against the SHA-256 below before it is installed in /opt/ai-arty/models.

- Smart Turn v3.2 (end-of-turn detection), smart-turn-v3.2-cpu.onnx, BSD 2-Clause, by Daily
  https://huggingface.co/pipecat-ai/smart-turn-v3 at revision f766f81d3cfdf7737ac64aad813d91bbfd56bf93
  sha256 2bb026316b14a660486a75b1733cd3fbab8c2fd0314dc9af7be49f8cca967e4f
- Silero VAD v6.2.3 (voice activity detection), silero_vad.onnx, MIT, by the Silero Team
  https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad/blob/v6.2.3/src/silero_vad/data/silero_vad.onnx
  sha256 1a153a22f4509e292a94e67d6f9b85e8deb25b4988682b7e174c65279d8788e3
- Moonshine tiny streaming English (speech to text), MIT, by Useful Sensors, Inc. (dba Moonshine AI), run with the
  moonshine-voice 0.1.6 Python package (MIT)
  https://download.moonshine.ai/model/tiny-streaming-en/quantized_26_11_02, eight files whose SHA-256s are pinned in
  fetch-models.sh

These are stored in this repository, in models/hey-arty:

- speech_embedding.onnx: Google's speech_embedding model (https://tfhub.dev/google/speech_embedding/1, TensorFlow 1
  version, Apache License 2.0, https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0), converted to ONNX without changes to
  its weights by wake-training/convert_embedding.py.
- hey_arty.npz: the "Hey Arty" classifier, trained for this project by wake-training/train_spotter.py on speech made
  with the Kokoro-82M text-to-speech model (Apache License 2.0, https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M) run through
  kokoro-onnx (MIT). No openWakeWord models or data were used.

